[["NSE vs BSE (simulated): the same share on India's two exchanges, minute by minute. If you already hold a share, sell it where it's dearer and buy the same number back where it's cheaper; your holding is unchanged and you keep the gap, minus costs. No orders are placed."], ["Costs for a Rs 1,00,000 trade: holdings route (sell from demat, buy back, STT both sides) 0.239%; intraday route (only if your broker lets the legs offset) 0.083%. A gap smaller than that loses money. Trade size: Rs 1,00,000 or what traded on each exchange that minute, whichever is smaller. Profits are an upper bound: the last trade of a minute may no longer be available."], [], ["Two measures: 'same minute' trades at the prices of the minute the gap shows (impossible by hand: the gap is usually two last trades up to a minute apart, and firms next to the exchange take it in milliseconds); 'next minute' places both orders in the following minute and gets that minute's prices, which is what someone watching a screen could do."], ["BY DAY", "Date", "Shares compared", "Minutes compared", "Median gap (%)", "Minutes above holdings cost", "Holdings: gaps", "Holdings: same minute (Rs)", "Holdings: next minute (Rs)", "Holdings: next-minute wins", "Intraday: gaps", "Intraday: same minute (Rs)", "Intraday: next minute (Rs)", "Intraday: next-minute wins"], ["", "'2026-11-27", 493, 113891, 0.0405, 628, 611, 40696.27, -48176.94, 11, 14744, 307409.59, -339697.88, 992], ["", "'2026-11-26", 493, 117442, 0.0415, 721, 695, 42839.08, -60440.87, 16, 16148, 335973.8, -381142.53, 1109], ["", "'2026-11-25", 493, 129002, 0.0405, 744, 720, 53425.42, -52220.43, 15, 17160, 384543.56, -435143.58, 1173], ["", "'2026-11-23", 493, 122292, 0.0395, 785, 763, 55906.18, -56249.44, 12, 16298, 368004.04, -398834.73, 1114], ["", "'2026-11-20", 493, 124285, 0.0385, 648, 639, 47881.0, -58052.77, 3, 15825, 348797.78, -411708.81, 1023], ["", "'2026-11-19", 493, 118614, 0.0417, 608, 592, 52322.23, -49542.2, 12, 15389, 338205.55, -372758